    <Label IsHitTestVisible="false" Name="Title" Style="GalleryTitle" Text="Ceva's Theorem" DecimalsToShow="2" X="6.417" Y="2.276" />
    <Label IsHitTestVisible="false" Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="Points D, E and F lie on the sides of triangle\nABC. When do the segments AD, BE and CF pass\nthrough a single point?\n\nExactly when this product of ratios equals 1:\nAF/FB · BD/DC · CE/EA = [AF/FB*BD/DC*CE/EA]\n\nDrag D, E and F until the three segments meet,\nand watch the number." DecimalsToShow="2" X="6.417" Y="0.948">
